      ],
      "text": [
        "ALDENMERE BEHIND. THE MERE AHEAD.",
        "Under that, scratched in later and not by the same hand: 'the cut is dry. dont drink from it.'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "npc",
      "tile": [
        12,
        20
      ],
      "tint": [
        0.8,
        0.9,
        1.0
      ],
      "text": [
        "The channel's been my job for thirty years. Keep it clear, keep it moving.",
        "It's clear. It isn't moving. You tell me which of those is my fault."
      ],
      "stage_text": [
        {
          "from": "the_road",
          "text": [
            "You're the one they sent up from the village. Good.",
            "This cut drains the mere south to Aldenmere. Thirty years I've kept it clear.",
            "It's clear now. And it's dry. Water doesn't stop unless something stops it.",
            "Whatever that is, it's up at the head, not down here. Go and look."
          ]
        },
        {
          "from": "the_shore",
          "text": [
            "You saw it, then. I can tell by your face.",
            "Thirty years I kept the cut clear, and the thing stopping it was never in the cut."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sets_stage": "the_sluice"
    },
    {
      "type": "sign",
      "tile": [
        16,
        10
      ],
      "text": [
        "The sluice gate. The frame is sound, the boards are sound, the mechanism turns.",
        "Below it the channel bed is grey and cracked and has been for some time.",
        "Nothing here is broken. That is the part that bothers you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spring",
      "tile": [
        18,
        10
      ],
      "text": [
        "A seep comes out of the bank beside the dead channel, thin and cold and perfectly clear.",
        "You wash the fen off and let your creatures drink. Whatever is wrong upstream has not reached this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "npc",
      "tile": [
        29,
        6
      ],
      "tint": [
        1.0,
        0.85,
        0.7
      ],
      "text": [
        "Don't go up to the shore at night. That's not superstition, that's the reeds.",
        "Things come out of them at level you're not ready for, and they don't scare."
      ],
      "stage_text": [
        {
          "from": "the_sluice",
          "text": [
            "Carting salt up to the mere, same as every week. Nobody's buying it.",
            "Whole shore's gone quiet. Not empty -- quiet. There's a difference and you'll hear it."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
